.TH elfshaker-esi 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-esi \- Create and edit elfshaker remote indexes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker esi\fR [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create and edit remote index (.esi) files. A remote index is a small published catalog used by clone and update. It tells clients where to find packs and how to verify them. The v1 format records checksums; v2 also records byte sizes. These commands edit explicitly named local files; they do not use an elfshaker data directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
elfshaker\-esi\-create(1)
Create an empty remote index
.TP
elfshaker\-esi\-list(1)
List entries in a remote index
.TP
elfshaker\-esi\-add(1)
Add packs to one or more remote indexes
.TP
elfshaker\-esi\-remove(1)
Remove pack URLs from one or more remote indexes
.SH EXAMPLES
Create compatible v1 and v2 indexes, then add one pack to both:
.PP
.nf
\fBelfshaker esi create \-\-meta v1 \-\-url https://example.test/index.esi index.esi\fR
.br
\fBelfshaker esi create \-\-meta v2 \-\-url https://example.test/index.v2.esi index.v2.esi\fR
.br
\fBelfshaker esi add \-\-also index.esi index.v2.esi release.pack\fR
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
elfshaker\-esi\-create(1), elfshaker\-esi\-list(1), elfshaker\-esi\-add(1), elfshaker\-esi\-remove(1), elfshaker\-clone(1), elfshaker\-update(1)
